  clock: 4  # 6473
  nonce: '6473'  # 6473
  message: "Second outside-reader review, 2026-11-13 (self-run cache f36c63310c791188/results/c872eb7a7e793eab/ac34c56c06ec1788, re-checked on dev fed15705d7, 20 other repositories measured; ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/outside_reader_review2_11142026). NEW INSTANCE on the self-run: the ten highest CLI entries all have rank_score exactly 1.0 (a main_function at base 0.8 and a cli_command at base 0.99 both clamp), so their order is the tie-break: language weight, then effective out-degree. The console scripts declared in [project.scripts] (hypergumbo-tracker, htrac, hypergumbo, hypergumbo-tracker-textconv) are symbols of language toml, whose weight is near zero, so they come 7th to 10th, under every saturated Python main including the main of a recorded test-input project (6th). The tracker's main is first and the core main second on effective out-degree (380 against 89). A reader saw this as 'the hypergumbo console script is ninth, below the tracker's main'. So the highest-confidence statement a repository makes about its own commands ranks last among the ties. Read from the entrypoints of the full survey."  # 6473
- op: discuss  # 3c7b
  at: '2026-11-14T09:47:52Z'  # 3c7b
  by: agent  # 3c7b
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 3c7b
  clock: 5  # 3c7b
  nonce: 3c7b  # 3c7b
  message: "WHY PR #2183 DOES NOT TOUCH THIS. The ties come from the clamp at 1.0 and from the boost's own cap (0.25, reached at 11 effective edges). Removing either is not a local fix: docs/schema.json bounds Entrypoint.rank_score at 1.0, and ADR-0039 ruling 3 moves the ranking adjustments to rank_score 'unchanged in formula and magnitude'. A formula that keeps the base order of detection kinds under the bound (rank = base + (1 - base) x boost share) still ties at 1.0 once the boost is saturated. So this needs a ruling on the rank formula, then a measurement of the entry order on a corpus."  # 3c7b
